# hugmesh-tor-reconcile — Tor v3 onion-service refresh timer (24h default).
#
# The TIMER half of the onion-service reconcile (the OpenRC oneshot runs the agent
# once at boot; this file re-runs it). cronie reads /etc/cron.d (the same mechanism
# the egress-VPN + backup + device-registry-sync timers use). Installed ONLY when the
# 'tor' optional service is selected (PR gate).
#
# The agent is FAIL-SOFT + idempotent: the v3 onion keypair is minted once, by tor,
# on first boot and PERSISTS (off-git, tor:tor) so the .onion address is stable.
#
# @reboot — the boot oneshot runs BEFORE tor and never starts it (a nested start
# would stall the boot on the oneshot's own OpenRC lock), so on the FIRST boot no
# keypair exists yet when it exits. This run, after a delay, finds tor running (OpenRC
# started it after the oneshot), waits for the fresh keypair and EXPORTS the hostname
# — without it the first-boot hostname would appear only at the next midnight run.
# If tor is somehow still down by then, this run (no RC_SVCNAME) starts it.
# daily   — re-asserts the managed torrc, starts a stopped/crashed tor (this also
# restarts a tor an admin stopped by hand) and re-exports the hostnames.
#
# Field order: min hour dom month dow user command
@reboot root sleep 90; /usr/sbin/hugmesh-tor-reconcile >> /var/log/hugmesh-tor-reconcile.log 2>&1
0 0 * * * root /usr/sbin/hugmesh-tor-reconcile >> /var/log/hugmesh-tor-reconcile.log 2>&1
